```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

const SUBSCRIPTIONS_KEY: &str = "subscriptions";

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get(SUBSCRIPTIONS_KEY) {
            Some(raw) => parse_urls(&raw),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

/// The stored value holds one subscription URL per line. Blank lines and
/// surrounding whitespace are dropped.
fn parse_urls(raw: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    raw.lines()
        .map(str::trim)
        .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
        .map(String::from)
        .collect()
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read`, so it has no authority to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or to call `https://metadata.internal.example`. A `wasm32-unknown-unknown` build has no filesystem access anyway. The metadata call would also send the input's text to an external host, which changes what data leaves the node. If operations wants either behaviour, it needs to be granted explicitly through the node's capabilities, or handled outside this node.

